<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khatyn massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khatyn massacre was the destruction of the village of Khatyn in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> by a German auxiliary police battalion and SS troops on 22 March 1943. Its 149 inhabitants, including 75 children, were burned in a barn or shot in reprisal for a partisan attack. A memorial complex opened on the site in 1969 commemorates them and the hundreds of other Belarusian villages destroyed during the occupation.</p></div>
